        "original_id": "eb98f255-03b4-528b-a2b8-ddcb9fce245a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Nick Grindé, Karel Reisz, Hylda Baker, Tony Richardson\n- Works: Saturday Night and Sunday Morning\n- Places: Britain, Farnworth, Lancashire\n- Topics: British cinema, post-World War II film\n\nFacts:\n- Nick Grindé was born on January 12, 1893, and he became an American film director and screenwriter.\n- Karel Reisz was born on July 21, 1926, and he became a British filmmaker active in post-World War II Britain.\n- During the 1950s and 1960s, Karel Reisz was one of the pioneers of the new realist strain in British cinema.\n- In 1960, the British drama film Saturday Night and Sunday Morning was directed by Karel Reisz and produced by Tony Richardson.\n- In 1960, Hylda Baker appeared in the film Saturday Night and Sunday Morning.\n- From 1968 to 1973, Hylda Baker was known for playing Nellie Pledge in the ITV sitcom Nearest and Dearest.\n- Hylda Baker was born and brought up in Farnworth, Lancashire.\n- Nick Grindé died on June 19, 1979.\n- Karel Reisz died on November 25, 2002.",
